approve Plugin for DokuWiki

Page approval mechanism for dokuwiki.

Approval variables (where approval is enabled):

  * @APPROVE_VERSION@ — approved major/minor version.
  * @APPROVE_DATE@ — approval date, using the wiki's date format.
  * @APPROVE_USER@ — approving user's username.
  * @APPROVE_NAME@ — approving user's current full name from the authentication
    backend, falling back to the username if the name/account is unavailable.
  * @APPROVE_MESSAGE@ — the Approval Message saved with the displayed revision.
    Empty for approved revisions without a message, including older approvals.

The approval comparison screen has an optional Approval Message beside the
Approve Major/Minor buttons. Messages are plain text (up to 4000 characters),
with line breaks preserved, and belong to that approval rather than a wiki edit.
They are not automatically filled from edit summaries. The message variable also
works in PDF exports. Drafts and previews show TBD, as with other approval variables.

Approval is submitted using a CSRF-protected POST form and checks the reviewed
revision is still current. Old direct approval GET links no longer approve pages.
Database update 5 adds a nullable message column; existing approvals are retained.
Nonempty approval messages also appear in Old Revisions and below the corresponding
diff headings. The approval banner stays compact and does not show messages.
Original edit summaries are retained. Empty messages add no UI elements.

Approval review compares the last approved revision with the current draft. For
the first approval, the whole page is shown as new content. Differences views
for editors label approved versions and drafts in the revision selectors, and
list the edit summaries after the older revision through the newer revision
(inclusive). Changing the comparison updates this list; approval is offered only
when the comparison includes the current unapproved revision. Core diff rendering
is reused, with no changes to DokuWiki or the Changes plugin.

Page history syntax (for the current page):

---- approve history ----
from: 1.0
to: 3.0
show: all
----

This lists edit summaries and any approved versions with their approval messages
AFTER version 1.0 THROUGH version 3.0. The starting revision is excluded, matching
the diff view. Edit authors/dates and approval authors/dates are shown separately.
All intervening approvals are included, not only the final one.

For a release history with only approved versions and their messages:

---- approve history ----
show: approvals
order: oldest
----

Options:
  * from/to: approval versions such as 1.0 or v1.0, or rev:1700000000 for an exact
    revision timestamp. Unknown versions/options produce an error, not an unfiltered list.
  * Omitting from starts before the first revision. Omitting to (or using current)
    ends at the revision being viewed. Old revisions never include later history.
  * show: all (default) or approvals. Approval-only lists omit all edit summaries.
  * order: newest (default) or oldest.

No page or namespace parameter is supported. Read access and the draft-visibility
rules apply; readers who cannot see drafts cannot list history beyond the latest
approved revision. Empty approval messages add no message element, but the approved
version is still listed. The list uses ordinary HTML, without JavaScript or a new
database table, and shares its lookup/rendering code with the diff history panel.
Pages with history syntax bypass the rendered HTML cache to reflect approvals and
viewer permissions. Approval also touches existing page metadata to invalidate
dependent exports such as DW2PDF.

Unapproved revisions and edit previews show TBD. The full name is looked up
when rendering, not stored in the approval database; this also applies to old
approved revisions. After changing a user's name, a cached page may need purging
before the new name appears.

All documentation for this plugin can be found at
https://www.dokuwiki.org/plugin:approve

If you install this plugin manually, make sure it is installed in
lib/plugins/approve/ - if the folder is called different it
will not work!

Please refer to http://www.dokuwiki.org/plugins for additional info
on how to install plugins in DokuWiki.

